		'explanation' => 'Why A is correct: These elements help the client understand the service, make a voluntary decision, anticipate financial and privacy issues, and recognize the circumstances in which confidentiality may be limited.\n\nWhy B is incorrect: Personal opinions or information about previous clients are irrelevant to the current client\'s decision and may create confidentiality and professionalism concerns.\n\nWhy C is incorrect: The clinician should explain the proposed service and relevant methods, not provide an exhaustive inventory of every technique learned. Excess information can obscure what the client actually needs to understand.\n\nWhy D is incorrect: Clinicians should discuss current assessment findings and uncertainty appropriately, but they cannot predict every future diagnosis. Informed consent should be accurate and relevant rather than speculative.\n\nCTA Clinical Takeaway: Give the client the information reasonably needed to understand the service and decide whether to participate.\n\nSource Alignment: Module 2; course Objective 2.',
